    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2YWjtKsLbFBfV3ynQseWxLE)_\n\n## What\n`vertico-posframe` no longer resizes to the prompt. `vertico-posframe-size-function` is now `sp-posframe-get-size`, which sets `:width`, `:min-width` and `:max-width` to `sp-posframe-width-fraction` (0.75) of the parent frame for every command, file pickers included. Height still fits the candidates. `vertico-posframe-min-width` is dropped. Doc and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n## Not tested\nNothing was run in Emacs (none in the container), and `vertico-posframe` is not installed here, so the plist keys returned by `vertico-posframe-get-size` and the size-function option are from memory of the package. Please check `M-x` and `find-file`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9cVX4xhp367pqb88n)_",
